<title>FRANCE: Workers strike for 24 hours in French port Nantes.</title>
<headline>Workers strike for 24 hours in French port Nantes.</headline>
<dateline>RENNES, France 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Workers in the western French port of Nantes-Saint Nazaire launched a 24-hour strike on Thursday to signal their opposition to any lay-offs.</p>
<p>Some 150 port workers gathered in front of the Saint Nazaire Chamber of Commerce during a meeting of the port authority's board of directors to demonstrate their concerns, a spokesman for the Communist-led CGT trade union said.</p>
<p>The port, which currently employs nearly 500 people, is reviewing its operations, and CGT officials said they feared the audit would be used as an excuse for redundancies.</p>
</text>
